How the hook environment differs, measured on this machine.
Both probes installed a temporary .git/hooks/pre-commit that did nothing but
dump its own environment, ran one --allow-empty commit, and were removed.

== A. ordinary commit: git commit --allow-empty -m ... ==
cwd=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter
GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=@1790405877 +0700
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=kietna.work@gmail.com
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=koniz-dev
GIT_EDITOR=:
GIT_EXEC_PATH=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/libexec/git-core
GIT_INDEX_FILE=.git/index
GIT_PREFIX=

GIT_DIR: absent. GIT_INDEX_FILE: relative. Nothing here can mislead the
Flutter SDK, which is why the hook has always worked in a plain clone.

== B. commit whose git directory is not the default $PWD/.git: ==
   git --git-dir="$PWD/.git" --work-tree="$PWD" commit --allow-empty -m ...
cwd=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter
GIT_AUTHOR_DATE=@1790406289 +0700
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=kietna.work@gmail.com
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=koniz-dev
GIT_DIR=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git
GIT_EDITOR=:
GIT_EXEC_PATH=/Applications/Xcode.app/Contents/Developer/usr/libexec/git-core
GIT_INDEX_FILE=/Users/nguyenanhkiet/Playground/flutter-starter/.git/index
GIT_PREFIX=
GIT_WORK_TREE=.

GIT_DIR: absolute, exported. GIT_WORK_TREE and an absolute GIT_INDEX_FILE
appear too. This is the shape a worktree hook runs in - a worktree's .git
is a file pointing at <main>/.git/worktrees/<name>, so git has to export
the resolved directory the same way.

This probe is how far this session could go without creating a worktree,
which it is instructed not to do on this repository. It establishes the
mechanism (git exports an absolute GIT_DIR once the git directory is not
the default) but not the literal worktree transcript criterion 1 asks for.
That one criterion is routed to status:needs-uat.
